 "exercises": [
  {
   "id": "a1",
   "source_id": "Finding the eigenvectors and eigenvalues of this matrix is again left to the reader",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "end"
   },
   "cite": "finding-the-states",
   "prompt": "<p>Two equivalent protons have Larmor frequency $\\nu = 300$ MHz and coupling constant $J = 7.0$ Hz. In frequency units, find (a) $E_2$ and (b) $E_3$ in Hz, and (c) $E_1 - E_2$ and (d) $E_2 - E_4$ in MHz.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "multi",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "parts": [
     {
      "part": "a",
      "value": 1.75,
      "unit": "Hz",
      "hint": "The triplet state |2⟩ has energy J/4."
     },
     {
      "part": "b",
      "value": -5.25,
      "unit": "Hz"
     },
     {
      "part": "c",
      "value": 300,
      "unit": "MHz"
     },
     {
      "part": "d",
      "value": 300,
      "unit": "MHz"
     }
    ],
    "solution": "<p>From the eigenvalues of the Hamiltonian matrix (14.7.5): $E_2 = J/4 = 7.0/4 = 1.75$ Hz and $E_3 = -3J/4 = -5.25$ Hz. With $E_1 = \\nu + J/4$ and $E_4 = -\\nu + J/4$, the two allowed transitions are $E_1 - E_2 = \\nu = 300$ MHz and $E_2 - E_4 = \\nu = 300$ MHz. The coupling shifts the levels but cancels from both differences, so the spectrum shows one line.</p>"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "a2",
   "source_id": "We have four different states, which leads to",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Understand",
   "place": {
    "at": "end"
   },
   "cite": "selection-rules",
   "prompt": "<p>Of the six possible transitions among the states $|1\\rangle$ to $|4\\rangle$ of two equivalent spin-$1/2$ nuclei, which does the selection rule $\\Delta I = 0$, $\\Delta M_I = \\pm 1$ allow?</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "choice",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "options": [
     "$|4\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |2\\rangle$ and $|2\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |1\\rangle$",
     "$|4\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |3\\rangle$ and $|3\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |1\\rangle$",
     "$|4\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |1\\rangle$ only",
     "all six"
    ],
    "correct": 0,
    "hint": "Read I and M_I for each state off the table of states.",
    "solution": "<p>$|1\\rangle$, $|2\\rangle$ and $|4\\rangle$ form the triplet ($I = 1$, $M_I = 1, 0, -1$) and $|3\\rangle$ is the singlet ($I = 0$). $\\Delta I = 0$ rules out every transition to or from $|3\\rangle$, and $\\Delta M_I = \\pm 1$ rules out $|4\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |1\\rangle$, which changes $M_I$ by 2. That leaves $|4\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |2\\rangle$ and $|2\\rangle \\leftrightarrow |1\\rangle$.</p>"
   }
  }
 ],
